Z||000001||longjonsilver||11-25-2001||12:05 PM||||id like to know too!  mine is too badly cracked to repair.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Earl:<BR><B> A tree limb took out my windsheild last night how hard are they to replace?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-25-2001||12:20 PM||||Let the experts replace it for you, that way you also get a warranty in case it leaks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||11-25-2001||07:11 PM||||if you will do a search of tech archives-Replacing windshield-as the search terms, you will find several entries. At least one gives the details of doing it yourself, one goes into remarks concerning the use of the windshield as structural integrity. Most follow Avengador's recommendation. The cost is not that much, and I would imagine it's a lot of work to get one out in one piece from a junkyard. I've done it on other vehicles, but not on a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-25-2001||07:36 PM||||Most yard wont pull glass, if you try and break it they still charge you from what Ive heard. You can get a brand new one, installed, for less than $150. Ive had 2 done here. Let me tell you, theres nothing as good as seeing thru brand new glass.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||11-26-2001||07:07 AM||||That's one of the things I have to replace on my Fiero when it comes home. Except they are $600 here. Other cars are much cheaper of course. But not the Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero4.gif">      <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
